Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:55:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 196/209] feat(area): spline creation and point-tool support

Create Object -> Area -> Spline, and the one change the shared point tool needed
in order to edit a curve without learning what a curve is.

CSplineCreateTool is a ~30-line subclass of the stage 1b CShapeCreateTool:
object class AreaShapeSpline, minimum two points (CSplineObject::GetMinPoints(),
SplineObject.h:83). Everything else - first click spawns the entity with its
shape component, further clicks append, double-click or Enter finishes, Esc
discards, the whole draw is one undo step - is the base tool unchanged. One tool
class per object class, because the Create panel hands a custom creation tool no
user data (report 02). CAreaShapeSplineClassDesc puts the entry in the panel.

CShapeEditTool gains one helper, GatherEdgePointsWorld(), which asks the kind
for the SHAPE of an edge through the new IShapeComponentEdit::GetEdgePoints()
and falls back to the chord when the kind answers 0 - which Box, Sphere and
Polygon all do by inheriting the default, so none of them changed. It is used in
exactly two places: the edge hit test now walks the edge's own samples, and the
Ctrl-hover highlight is drawn as that polyline instead of a straight line.

The effect is that Ctrl+click inserts a point ON the curve at the nearest place
rather than on the chord under it, and the highlighted segment follows the
curve - while the tool still never asks which kind of shape it is editing, which
is the rule stage 1 set for it. Insert, delete (never below two points; the
component refuses and warns) and drag ride the existing generic path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
